    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8b800724-4caa-5dfa-8df2-957704df0e8e",
      ":question/problem": "At which points on the curve $x^{2} + 2 x y=5 y + 6$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(2,-3)$\n- **II.** $(2,-2)$\n- **III.** $(1,-2)$\n- **IV.** $(3,-3)$\n- **V.** $(3,-2)$\n- **VI.** $(-3,-3)$\n- **VII.** $(-2,2)$",
